<title>USA: Toro Co files $250 mln debt, stock shelf.</title>
<headline>Toro Co files $250 mln debt, stock shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toro Co said Friday it filed a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $250 million in common stock debt securities, and warrants to purchase the debt and stock.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used for working capital and expansion of the business of the company and its subsidiaries, the filing said.</p>
<p>The Bloomington, Minn.,-based company is a manufacturer of consumer lawn mowers, snowthrowers, trimmers, commercial mowing and turf maintenance equipment and underground automatic irrigation systems.</p>
</text>
